# The operator's switch on the robot's state machine. Served by
# syncai_robot_state on the relative name `set_robot_state`, so it lands on
# <robot_id>/set_robot_state. The backend calls it for
# POST /api/v1/robot/state, the console's Confirm control (2026-11).
#
# It is the ONLY way into IDLE from UNINITIALIZED and the ONLY way out of
# ERROR. Nothing the stack does by itself confirms a position: a boot guess
# that converges on the last saved pose leaves the robot UNINITIALIZED until a
# person has looked at it.
#
#   state: RobotStatus.IDLE           "the robot is where the map shows it".
#          Refused NOT_CONVERGED unless the localizer's last guess has
#          converged (LocalizationStatus.converged) -- there is no estimate to
#          confirm otherwise. The confirmation is of that estimate: a map
#          switch or a new guess withdraws it (LocalizationStatus.pose_epoch).
#   state: RobotStatus.UNINITIALIZED  withdraw the confirmation. Never refused.
#
# Either one also releases a latched ERROR, and clears a task the robot still
# counts as running. The second is the recovery for a workflow terminated from
# outside, whose end_task never comes -- which is why this service does NOT
# refuse while a task runs. The caller does: the backend answers 409 while its
# own job list has a running job, and it is the one that knows.
#
# Any other value is refused INVALID_TARGET: RUNNING, ERROR, WARNING and
# CHARGING are derived, never commanded.
uint8 state
---
uint8 NONE           = 0
# IDLE asked for while the localizer has not converged, or has not been heard
# from at all (the mapping session runs no localizer).
uint8 NOT_CONVERGED  = 1
uint8 INVALID_TARGET = 2

bool success
uint8 code
# One English sentence, written for an operator.
string message
# The state the robot reports after the call (a RobotStatus value) -- on a
# refusal, the unchanged one. Note the rollup: a confirmed robot on its
# charger answers CHARGING, not IDLE.
uint8 state
